      "next_deadline": "No County NOFA found; confirm plan activities with Community and Economic Development (2222 M Street, Merced).",
      "prevailing_wage_trigger": "false",
      "layering_notes": "Merced County has no County housing finance program: the Community and Economic Development Department handles planning and the Housing Element, the Human Services Agency is Collaborative Applicant and Administrative Entity for the Merced City and County Continuum of Care (CA-520) and HHAP, Behavioral Health and Recovery Services holds BHSA, and the Housing Authority of the County of Merced (HACM) is the countywide PHA. The County is a non-entitlement jurisdiction for CDBG and HOME, has no housing trust fund, inclusionary ordinance, in-lieu fee or fee waiver, and Measure V (MCAG half-cent sales tax) is transportation only. The City of Merced is the entitlement jurisdiction with PLHA and Homekey awards (Pass 3). countyofmerced.com is Cloudflare-blocked to automated access (pages, DocumentCenter and AgendaCenter), so records were built from HCD tables and letters, mercedcoc.org reports, merced-pha.com, gocodebook (County Code Title 18) and press coverage; County documents are flagged for confirmation. Confirmation needed: at about $400,000 a year the County allocation could fund predevelopment or a small gap loan if the plan allows rental development, but the plan was not accessible. Source is HCD's 2024-2028 PLHA formula allocation NOFA tables.",
      "source_url": "https://www.hcd.ca.gov/sites/default/files/docs/grants-and-funding/plha/2024-2028-plha-formula-allocation-nofa.pdf",
